# Cloudflare Pages headers. The academy's live examples run in a frame on an opaque origin and
# fetch from here, so what they reach has to answer CORS. `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` is the
# other half of that: a page setting `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` blocks any
# cross-origin subresource that does not carry it, whatever CORS says.
#
# The runtime under /playground/_frontage/ is same-origin for the playground itself and needs
# neither, but it is served with both anyway: when the academy gains a `::: frontage` frame it
# will fetch exactly these files from exactly here, and a header that is already right is one
# fewer thing to debug through an opaque origin.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
/dist/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
/playground/_frontage/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
